  "id": "jarana_yucateca",
  "name": "Jarana yucateca (Yucatecan vaquería dance band)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The jarana is the couple dance of Yucatán, danced at the vaquerías of town and village fiestas in two meters, the 6/8 jarana and the 3/4 jarana, with pauses in which a dancer recites a bomba, a comic or amorous verse. It is played by the orquesta jaranera, a band of clarinets, saxophone, trumpets and trombone over timbales, güiro and double bass, and Mérida ensembles such as the Orquesta Jaranera del Mayab and the Orquesta Típica Yukalpetén have recorded it.",
  "recipe": "classic modern jarana yucateca, functional Song, Mexican branch. clarinet, trumpet, trombone, saxophone, timbales stick played, guiro, modern setup heavier bass bar kolstein bass specific double bass. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
